    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="6">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> 6</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="234" ed="#liebermann"/>Et precipimus, ne quis pecuniam puram et recte appendentem sonet, monetetur in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="56" target="#IVAtr_6.lnote.oe.56"/> quocumque portu monetetur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="57" target="#IVAtr_6.lnote.oe.57"/> in regno meo, super ouerhyrnessam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="58" target="#IVAtr_6.lnote.oe.58"/> meam.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="6" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="76" ed="#robertson"/>Et praecipimus ne quis pecuniam puram et recte appendentem sonet, monetetur in quocumque portu monetetur<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_6.robnote.fn.1"/> in regno meo, super overhirnessam meam.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="235" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wir gebieten, dass niemand reines und richtig wiegendes Geld zurückweise<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_6.lnote.de.1"/>, sei es geprägt, in welcher Stadt in meinem Reiche es auch geprägt sei, bei [Strafe der Busse für] Ungehorsam gegen mich.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And we command that no one refuse pure money of correct weight, wherever in my kingdom it may have been minted, on [pain of the fine for] disobedience to me.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="77" ed="#robertson"/>And we enjoin that no-one shall refuse pure money of the proper weight, in whatever town<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_6.robnote.n.1"/> in my kingdom it be coined, under pain of incurring the fine for insubordination to me.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="235"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_8">III Eg 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. III Eg. 8</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares III Eg 8.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_6.lnote.oe.56" n="56" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">234</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in q. p. m. <hi rend="italic">überspringt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in q. p. m. omitted by R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_6.lnote.oe.57" n="57" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">234</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">monetur <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">monetur MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_6.lnote.oe.58" n="58" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">234</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-hir. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-hir. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_6.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Im Orig. stand <hi rend="italic">forsace</hi>. Eine Beeinflussung durchs Kapitular von 794c. 5 scheint nicht ganz unmöglich: <hi rend="italic">in omni civitate denarii si nominis nostri nomisma habent et mero sunt argento, pleniter pensantes si quis contradicit eos</hi>. … Ich drucke <hi rend="spaced">klein</hi> inhaltlich Gleiches.—<hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Stadt 15; Ungehorsam 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The orig. read <hi rend="italic">forsace</hi>. Influence from the capitulary of 794c. 5 does not seem altogether impossible: <hi rend="italic">in omni civitate denarii si nominis nostri nomisma habent et mero sunt argento, pleniter pensantes si quis contradicit eos</hi>. … I print in <hi rend="italic">small type</hi> what is identical in content.—<hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Stadt 15; Ungehorsam 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_6.lnote.de.0" n="0" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Sachgemässer würde bei 6. 7. 8. 9 kein neues Kapitel begonnen.—</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">It would be more appropriate to the subject matter not to begin a new chapter at 6. 7. 8. 9.—</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_6.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">For a list of the places possessing a mint in the reign of Æthelred, see Powell, <hi rend="italic">E.H.R.</hi>, <hi rend="smallcaps">xi</hi>. p. 761.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IVAtr_6.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>monetetur</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">monetur</hi> M, Hk, Br; <hi rend="italic">in q. p. m.</hi> om. R.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
